meta {
  name: Weather by City ID
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  `GET /weather/city/{cityId:long}`

  Get weather by OpenWeatherMap city ID. The most precise lookup - use it to
  avoid the ambiguity of duplicate city names.

  | Param    | In    | Required | Default  | Notes                                |
  | -------- | ----- | -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |
  | `cityId` | path  | yes      | -        | OpenWeatherMap city ID (integer)     |
  | `units`  | query | no       | `Metric` | `Standard` \| `Metric` \| `Imperial` |
  | `lang`   | query | no       | -        | Two-letter language code             |

  The route only matches whole-number IDs, so `1.5` or `melbourne` is a `404`.

  City ID lists are published at http://bulk.openweathermap.org/sample/

  Melbourne (`7839805`) is the API's default city - see `Constants.DEFAULT_CITY_ID`,
  used by the legacy `GET /weather` endpoint and the nightly digest job.
}
